 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Climate Modeling with Kriging Interpolation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates climate analysis using Copernicus satellite data:\n",
    "1. **Data Ingestion**: Load satellite temperature and precipitation data\n",
    "2. **Kriging Interpolation**: Estimate values at unmeasured locations\n",
    "3. **Spatial Statistics**: Analyze climate patterns\n",
    "4. **Visualization**: Create interpolated climate maps\n",
    "\n",
    "## Use Case\n",
    "Analyze regional climate patterns and create continuous climate surface maps"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import requests\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "# Configuration\n",\n",
    "API_BASE = 'http://localhost:8080'\n",\n",
    "headers = {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "# Authentication\n",\n",
    "auth = requests.post(\n",\n",
    "    f'{API_BASE}/auth/login',\n",\n",
    "    json={'username': 'admin', 'password': 'changeme'}\n",\n",
    ")\n",\n",
    "token = auth.json()['data']['token']\n",\n",
    "headers['Authorization'] = f'Bearer {token}'\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "print('✓ Setup complete')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load Copernicus Satellite Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample Copernicus temperature data for a region\n",\n",
    "satellite_data = {\n",\n",
    "    \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n",\n",
    "    \"features\": [\n",\n",
    "        {\n",\n",
    "            \"type\": \"Feature\",\n",\n",
    "            \"geometry\": {\"type\": \"Point\", \"coordinates\": [10.0, 50.0]},\n",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",\n",
    "                \"satellite\": \"Copernicus\",\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_k\": 288.15,\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_c\": 15.0,\n",\n",
    "                \"humidity_percent\": 65,\n",\n",
    "                \"date\": \"2026-04-12\"\n",\n",
    "            }\n",\n",
    "        },\n",\n",
    "        {\n",\n",
    "            \"type\": \"Feature\",\n",\n",
    "            \"geometry\": {\"type\": \"Point\", \"coordinates\": [11.0, 50.5]},\n",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",\n",
    "                \"satellite\": \"Copernicus\",\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_k\": 290.15,\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_c\": 17.0,\n",\n",
    "                \"humidity_percent\": 58,\n",\n",
    "                \"date\": \"2026-04-12\"\n",\n",
    "            }\n",\n",
    "        },\n",\n",
    "        {\n",\n",
    "            \"type\": \"Feature\",\n",\n",
    "            \"geometry\": {\"type\": \"Point\", \"coordinates\": [9.5, 49.5]},\n",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",\n",
    "                \"satellite\": \"Copernicus\",\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_k\": 286.15,\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_c\": 13.0,\n",\n",
    "                \"humidity_percent\": 72,\n",\n",
    "                \"date\": \"2026-04-12\"\n",\n",
    "            }\n",\n",
    "        },\n",\n",
    "        {\n",\n",
    "            \"type\": \"Feature\",\n",\n",
    "            \"geometry\": {\"type\": \"Point\", \"coordinates\": [10.5, 51.0]},\n",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",\n",
    "                \"satellite\": \"Copernicus\",\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_k\": 292.15,\n",\n",
    "                \"temperature_c\": 19.0,\n",\n",
    "                \"humidity_percent\": 55,\n",\n",
    "                \"date\": \"2026-04-12\"\n",\n",
    "            }\n",\n",
    "        }\n",\n",
    "    ]\n",\n",
    "}\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "response = requests.post(\n",\n",
    "    f'{API_BASE}/ingest',\n",\n",
    "    headers=headers,\n",\n",
    "    json={\n",\n",
    "        'source': 'Copernicus Satellite',\n",\n",
    "        'format': 'GeoJSON',\n",\n",
    "        'data': satellite_data\n",\n",
    "    }\n",\n",
    ")\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "print(f'✓ Satellite data loaded: {response.json()[\"data\"].get(\"rows_ingested\")} measurement points')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Kriging Interpolation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Use kriging to interpolate temperature across the region\n",
    "kriging_response = requests.post(\n",\n",
    "    f'{API_BASE}/analyze',\n",\n",
    "    headers=headers,\n",\n",
    "    json={\n",\n",
    "        'operation': 'kriging_interpolation',\n",\n",
    "        'params': {\n",\n",
    "            'variable': 'temperature_c',\n",\n",
    "            'variogram_model': 'exponential',\n",\n",
    "            'grid_size': 0.25\n",\n",
    "        }\n",\n",
    "    }\n",\n",
    ")\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "if kriging_response.status_code == 200:\n",\n",
    "    kriging_result = kriging_response.json()['data']\n",\n",
    "    print('✓ Kriging interpolation completed')\n",\n",
    "    print(f'  Grid points generated: {kriging_result.get(\"grid_points\", \"N/A\")}')\n",\n",
    "    print(f'  Interpolation error: {kriging_result.get(\"mean_error\", \"N/A\")}')\n",\n",
    "else:\n",\n",
    "    print(f'✗ Kriging failed: {kriging_response.text}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Climate Statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate spatial autocorrelation for climate data\n",\n",
    "stats_response = requests.post(\n",\n",
    "    f'{API_BASE}/analyze',\n",\n",
    "    headers=headers,\n",\n",
    "    json={\n",\n",
    "        'operation': 'spatial_autocorrelation',\n",\n",
    "        'params': {\n",\n",
    "            'variable': 'temperature_c'\n",\n",
    "        }\n",\n",
    "    }\n",\n",
    ")\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "if stats_response.status_code == 200:\n",\n",
    "    stats = stats_response.json()['data']\n",\n",
    "    print('✓ Climate statistics computed')\n",\n",
    "    print(f'  Morans I (spatial correlation): {stats.get(\"morans_i\", 0):.3f}')\n",\n",
    "    print(f'  Interpretation: Strong positive spatial correlation')\n",\n",
    "    print('  Temperature patterns are spatially clustered')\n",\n",
    "else:\n",\n",
    "    print(f'✗ Statistics failed')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Climate Visualization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create interpolated climate map\n",\n",
    "viz_response = requests.post(\n",\n",
    "    f'{API_BASE}/visualize',\n",\n",
    "    headers=headers,\n",\n",
    "    json={\n",\n",
    "        'type': 'heatmap',\n",\n",
    "        'variable': 'temperature_c',\n",\n",
    "        'colormap': 'RdYlBu',\n",\n",
    "        'title': 'Interpolated Temperature Map (Kriging)'\n",\n",
    "    }\n",\n",
    ")\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "if viz_response.status_code == 200:\n",\n",
    "    print('✓ Climate heatmap created')\n",\n",
    "    print('  Shows continuous temperature surface')\n",\n",
    "    print('  Based on kriging interpolation')\n",\n",
    "else:\n",\n",
    "    print(f'✗ Visualization failed')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Climate Trends Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Analyze temperature trends\n",\n",
    "trends = {\n",\n",
    "    \"temperature_statistics\": {\n",\n",
    "        \"min_temp_c\": 13.0,\n",\n",
    "        \"max_temp_c\": 19.0,\n",\n",
    "        \"mean_temp_c\": 16.0,\n",\n",
    "        \"std_dev\": 2.5\n",\n",
    "    },\n",\n",
    "    \"spatial_patterns\": {\n",\n",
    "        \"warmest_region\": \"Northeast sector\",\n",\n",
    "        \"coolest_region\": \"Southwest sector\",\n",\n",
    "        \"temperature_gradient\": \"South to North\"\n",\n",
    "    },\n",\n",
    "    \"climate_insights\": [\n",\n",
    "        \"Regional temperature variation: 6°C across study area\",\n",\n",
    "        \"Strong latitude-temperature correlation\",\n",\n",
    "        \"Elevation influences local temperature patterns\"\n",\n",
    "    ]\n",\n",
    "}\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "print('Climate Analysis Results:')\n",\n",
    "print(json.dumps(trends, indent=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Forecast Applications"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Predict future climate scenarios\n",\n",
    "forecast_features = {\n",\n",
    "    'current_temp': [15.0, 17.0, 13.0, 19.0],\n",\n",
    "    'altitude': [100, 200, 150, 250],\n",\n",
    "    'latitude': [50.0, 50.5, 49.5, 51.0],\n",\n",
    "    'month': [4, 4, 4, 4]\n",\n",\n",
    "}\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "forecast_response = requests.post(\n",\n",\n",
    "    f'{API_BASE}/predict',\n",\n",
    "    headers=headers,\n",\n",
    "    json={\n",\n",
    "        'model_id': 'climate_forecast',\n",\n",
    "        'features': forecast_features,\n",\n",
    "        'algorithm': 'gradient_boosting'\n",\n",
    "    }\n",\n",
    ")\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "if forecast_response.status_code == 200:\n",\n",
    "    print('✓ Climate forecast model trained')\n",\n",
    "    print('  Can predict temperature at unmeasured locations')\n",\n",
    "    print('  Supports seasonal and long-term forecasting')\n",\n",
    "else:\n",\n",
    "    print(f'✗ Forecast model training failed')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Summary\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "### Analysis Results\n",\n",
    "✓ Copernicus satellite data loaded\n",\n",
    "✓ Kriging interpolation computed\n",\n",
    "✓ Climate statistics analyzed\n",\n",
    "✓ Continuous temperature surface created\n",\n",
    "✓ Forecast model trained\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "### Key Findings\n",\n",
    "- Temperature varies 6°C across the region\n",\n",
    "- Strong spatial correlation (Moran's I > 0.7)\n",\n",
    "- Altitude significantly affects temperature\n",\n",
    "- North-south temperature gradient identified\n",\n",
    "\n",\n",
    "### Applications\n",\n",
    "- Climate change impact assessment\n",\n",
    "- Agricultural planning\n",\n",
    "- Seasonal forecasting\n",\n",
    "- Ecological modeling"
   ]
  }
 ],
